highsea's Docker image: programs from Debian
============================================

The image is built on Debian 13 (trixie) and installs these Debian packages unmodified, from
Debian's own archive, with apt. highsea runs them as separate programs; it doesn't link them.

  Package          License        What highsea uses it for
  wireguard-tools  GPL-2.0        `wg`: sets the WireGuard keys and peer of highsea connects
  iproute2         GPL-2.0        `ip`: the interface, address, routes and rule of highsea connects
  wireguard-go     MIT            WireGuard in user space, where the kernel has none

Each package's copyright and full license text are in the image, at
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright. The exact version of each is what `dpkg -s <package>` reports
inside the image.

Source code offer
-----------------

The complete corresponding source code of every Debian package in the image, at the exact version
the image carries, is available from Debian:

  - https://sources.debian.org/src/<package>/<version>/
  - https://snapshot.debian.org/package/<package>/<version>/ (every version Debian has published)
  - or `apt-get source <package>` with a deb-src line for trixie.

For three years from the date an image is published, the highsea project will also provide that
source on request, for no more than the cost of providing it. Ask through the project's issue
tracker, naming the image's tag and the package.

highsea's own source is under AGPL-3.0-only, in the repository the image was built from.
